                <pb facs="0445" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg337"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-04-06"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Julian</hi>: In returning to you the Earl
                    of Rosebery’s dispatch of the 11th ultimo, which you kindly left with me,
                    relative to the reports received by Her Majesty’s Government respecting the
                    destruction of the American college at Massouvan, I beg you to convey to his
                    lordship my cordial thanks for his courtesy in communicating the information in
                    question to me.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
